 ],
 "balloons": [
  {
   "panel": "page-01-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Walk with me, Sawant.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-01-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "You do not have to go closer. The god knows you have your own ways.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-01-panel-05",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "Gods and I have an understanding. I try not to waste their time.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Watch instead.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Who pays for the oil in those lamps?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-01",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "The temple. From offerings.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN (off)"
   ],
   "text": "Where do the offerings come from?",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "From the fields. From houses like Padmini Amma's.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "And who pays when the temple roof leaks? When the priest demands new ornaments for the god? When the elephant that carries the idol in procession goes lame?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "The king. If he is wise.",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "If he wants men to believe the god favours his reign.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "A temple is not just stone. It is a ledger. Offerings in. Blessings out.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-01",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "The names written on both sides matter.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN (off)"
   ],
   "text": "Each of those lamps is paid for by a house.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN (off)"
   ],
   "text": "When the king asks for extra tax to pay for muskets and forts, they remember whether he feeds their god.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Do you see the pattern?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "I see men arguing over coins. That is the same everywhere.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-02",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Look closer.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "YUSUF"
   ],
   "text": "If your pepper is worm eaten, my mast will refuse to carry it. The Dutch will not pay for rot.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "yusuf"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-05-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "WOMAN"
   ],
   "text": "My pepper has fewer worms than your honesty.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-05-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "WOMAN"
   ],
   "text": "Your ships carry news as well as goods. When you bring Dutch coins into our land, remember that the king counts them with his fingers, not yours.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-05-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "The king's tax sits between them.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan",
    "yusuf"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-05-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Too high, the Marakkar captain goes to another coast. Too low, the palace cannot buy Dutch guns to shoot back at Dutch ships.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan",
    "yusuf"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "A diwan who hears only petitions in the court knows half a kingdom.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "The other half lives here, in the way people say 'our pepper' and 'the king's pepper,' as if they are the same, or as if they are not.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "DRILL MASTER"
   ],
   "text": "Ram, my friend! You come to see how well they march?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "I come to see whether they can do more than march.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-02",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "DRILL MASTER"
   ],
   "text": "One thing at a time. First they learn left from right.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Adequate.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "Praise indeed.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Our men must learn this European dance, or they will die confused when the Dutch play their drums.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "Do you want to sit on them? If the boat sinks, the fish will have a feast and the Dutch will laugh.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "Diwanji. Sawant. Come to see how your horses eat?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "Horses do not like water. I admire anyone who rides it as if it were a road.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "Water is a road. A road no company can draw a line through.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "They can put forts on the banks, but the backwaters go where they wish.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Pepper.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-04",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "And a little cardamom. Enough to flavour a Dutchman's breath and his profits.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-04",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "And for the king?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "His share is already in his godowns.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-05",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "I am not fool enough to cheat the man whose scribes have longer memories than my own mother.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Horses carry men to battle. Boats carry the coin that pays for their feed.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Temples carry the stories that make those men willing to die. Markets carry the arguments over who deserves what.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "For the Maharaja, conquest is not only taking land. It is knitting these pieces together, so that when a Dutch cannon fires at one place, the rest does not unravel.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "He is already at war. Even when the Dutch have not fired.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-10-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "He has been at war since before he took the throne.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-10-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "The Lords of the Eight Houses. The temple yogakkar who thought the gods answered only to them. They sent assassins as often as petitions.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-10-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Only after those knots were cut could he reach outward. Toward Kayamkulam. Then toward Dutch cannon.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-10-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Men like you feel war when the drums beat. Men like him feel it when the accounts do not balance.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-11-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "You have a sharp eye, Sawant. You see angles on a battlefield. See these angles too.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-11-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "When the time comes, the Maharaja will expect you to ride in ways that suit them. Not only your own.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-11-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "He has my sword. My eyes he can borrow when he asks.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-11-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Borrowed eyes.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-11-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "We will see how long he keeps the loan.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-12-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "You see? I do not destroy them because I hate them.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "varma",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-12-panel-05",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "I break them so they can be reset into a stronger bone.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "varma",
    "kayal"
   ]
  }
 ]
}